{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul","id":1470352,"title":"Hecata vs Path of Death and Soul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-13T10:10:41-08:00","id":1470352,"title":"Hecata vs Path of Death and Soul","content":"I have a question for more experienced Vampire players.<br /> How do You see Hecata and Sabbat path ? Similarities? <br /> Aren't they not so different? Or I don't see something obvious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T11:10:06-08:00","id":1470358,"title":"","content":"Hecata members should really just join the Camarilla or the Sabbat. No (good) reason to stand apart anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T12:28:03-08:00","id":1470362,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, the Giovanni (and Cappadocians before them) used to follow the Path of Bones, while the Sabbat followed the Path of Death and the Soul.<br /> <br /> So while the Path of Death and the Soul might be known to the Hecata, it's probably not the dominant Path for its members. The Nagaraja would probably be following one of the Paths associated with the True Black Hand which could include Death and the Soul, but would also include others like the Paths of Lilith, Scorched Heart, or Self Focus.<br /> <br /> And simply because these bloodlines are associated with some variant of Necromancy does not mean that all, or even most, of their members follow a Path of Enlightenment geared towards death and the dead. Those would just be more likely here than elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 12-26-2021, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T21:49:45-08:00","id":1470409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470358#post1470358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hecata members should really just join the Camarilla or the Sabbat. No (good) reason to stand apart anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have their own sect now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T02:39:47-08:00","id":1470413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470409#post1470409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have their own sect now.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there you have it from the horse's mouth...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T04:33:04-08:00","id":1470418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470358#post1470358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hecata members should really just join the Camarilla or the Sabbat. No (good) reason to stand apart anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But they work wonderfully as Independents! I'd argue even in favour of making them even more Sect and less Clan: it has always bugged me that Undead creatures didn't have a broad Sect / Religion based on understanding Death. They could also reap the fruits of the Sabbat difficulties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T05:02:56-08:00","id":1470421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470418#post1470418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they work wonderfully as Independents! I'd argue even in favour of making them even more Sect and less Clan: it has always bugged me that Undead creatures didn't have a broad Sect / Religion based on understanding Death. They could also reap the fruits of the Sabbat difficulties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I still do V20 for my games, this is entirely how I treat the Hecata\u2026 there was nothing mystical about The Family Reunion in the sense of merging bloodlines or other weirdness; it was the invocation of a Covenant between all the various clans/bloodlines of Death into a new Sect/Cult. The Giovanni are still Giovanni, the Skulls still Skulls, the Samedi and Nagaraja still Samedi and Nagaraja\u2026 but they have all pledged themselves to the Hecata cause with the ostensible Giovanni Antediluvian as the blood sacrifice that consecrated their cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T06:48:57-08:00","id":1470427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470418#post1470418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they work wonderfully as Independents! I'd argue even in favour of making them even more Sect and less Clan: it has always bugged me that Undead creatures didn't have a broad Sect / Religion based on understanding Death. They could also reap the fruits of the Sabbat difficulties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being their own Cult of Death doesn't stop them from joining a political faction. Remaining their own thing by now just doesn't make a lot of sense to me, even while I buy the Family Reunion itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T06:59:51-08:00","id":1470428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470427#post1470427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being their own Cult of Death doesn't stop them from joining a political faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, in &quot;Trails of Ash and Bones&quot; we have the Hecata slowly subverting the Camarilla structure in Florence: I do think that the Hecata can give us better plot hooks if they work along the Sects, but with their own cultish agenda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470427#post1470427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Remaining their own thing by now just doesn't make a lot of sense to me, even while I buy the Family Reunion itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The risk is surely of running into the Kyasid problem, &quot;<i>I just sit there and read for the next 300 years</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> An idea I've always toyed with, is a Deat Cult vampire sect uninterested in the mortal world: the Hecata could be their own political engine, but with their politics more concerned with the Underworld politics - the most they want from other Kindreds is being left alone and snatch interesting artifacts and materials for their experiments.<br /> <br /> IDK how they would work, surely the would have crossover potential.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T08:12:27-08:00","id":1470437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470427#post1470427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being their own Cult of Death doesn't stop them from joining a political faction. Remaining their own thing by now just doesn't make a lot of sense to me, even while I buy the Family Reunion itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how they benefit at all from joining when they have their own power block. What does joining the Camarilla or Anarchs give them when they can control their own cities now?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T08:37:35-08:00","id":1470439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470437#post1470437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how they benefit at all from joining when they have their own power block. What does joining the Camarilla or Anarchs give them when they can control their own cities now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Division of labour. <br /> <br /> The Cam works magnificently mostly because most of the clans are very specialized, which makes for a good economy. The Ventrue offer completely different services than the Nosferatu. A Hecata city where everyone has the same skillset just means people have nothing to sell and nothing to buy. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, like, the Tremere function pretty well as a sect within a sect. There's precedent; no reason why it can't be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T08:39:39-08:00","id":1470440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470439#post1470439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Division of labour.<br /> <br /> The Cam works magnificently mostly because most of the clans are very specialized, which makes for a good economy. The Ventrue offer completely different services than the Nosferatu. A Hecata city where everyone has the same skillset just means people have nothing to sell and nothing to buy.<br /> <br /> Also, like, the Tremere function pretty well as a sect within a sect. There's precedent; no reason why it can't be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hecata have a bigger cushion than the Camarilla due to the fact that they have families that specialize in much the same way as Clans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T08:57:12-08:00","id":1470442,"title":"","content":"Bigger what now? I don't mean to be rude but... do you think these responses through? Let's say there's two corpse-friendly families, Acata and Bacata... and they agree to get involved in different fields... how would this be any better than Ventrue and Nosferatu, or even Ventrue A and Ventrue B? Sure Acata can get into Banking and Bacata can get into megachurches... but what stops Acata getting into religion or Bacata getting in on finance? The two families have the same talent with little deviation, at most maybe a Discipline. The two families are direct competitors even if on the surface they agree not to get involved in some areas, but when banking goes big and megachurches get scrutinized, any chance of a friendly relationship with well defined boundries is over. The Cam has REAL diversity so it can easily overcome such issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T09:36:48-08:00","id":1470445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470442#post1470442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think these responses through?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a very strong vision of the clans but not all of us agree with it. The games also often disagree with the presentation you make. It's perfectly fine to forward your own view in lieu of canon but I feel like you act like they are canon sometimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's say there's two corpse-friendly families, Acata and Bacata... and they agree to get involved in different fields... how would this be any better than Ventrue and Nosferatu, or even Ventrue A and Ventrue B? Sure Acata can get into Banking and Bacata can get into megachurches... but what stops Acata getting into religion or Bacata getting in on finance? The two families have the same talent with little deviation, at most maybe a Discipline. The two families are direct competitors even if on the surface they agree not to get involved in some areas, but when banking goes big and megachurches get scrutinized, any chance of a friendly relationship with well defined boundries is over. The Cam has REAL diversity so it can easily overcome such issues. </div> </div> </div>The answer is pretty obvious that they are more likely to work for the Hecata than their own interests. Mind you, we've had the discussion about how the Camarilla's infighting is far far less in your vision of them than is in canon.<br /> <br /> Joining the Camarilla won't automatically make the Ventrue and Nosferatu allies of the Hecata versus their own people doing the same jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-14-2021, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T09:39:34-08:00","id":1470446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470428#post1470428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The risk is surely of running into the Kyasid problem, &quot;<i>I just sit there and read for the next 300 years</i>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was Cappadocius thing way before the Kiasyd, but I don't see the Heata going that way for a simple reason: they're already driven on more material arenas.<br /> <br /> Giovanni deals with money, Nagaraja with temple protection and maintenance, Samedi sell their magic for money and influence. The Samedi also were already making formal contact with the Camarilla. One way or another, they're all more politically invested than the Cappadocian ever was, so I fully expect them to be more than just a death cult focused on reading books for centuries at a time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470437#post1470437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how they benefit at all from joining when they have their own power block. What does joining the Camarilla or Anarchs give them when they can control their own cities now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three things:<br /> <br /> 1 - Stability. By joining forces with another block they avoid having to defend their cities alone. For now they can just let the world burn, but sooner or later someone will come for their cities and they'll have to fend off invasion;<br /> <br /> 2 - Avoiding administrative responsibilities. As I see them, they have little if any interest on directly ruling cities other than Venice. They have their businesses, cult and research to focus, already a lot on their hands without the burden of being actual Princes and whatnot;<br /> <br /> 3 - Playing the long game. They're all bloodlines used to far reaching political agendas played behind the back of the Powers That Be instead of disputing titles. Disinterested from offices, yet far from politically inactive. As they are now, they lack rulers and populations they can use other than themselves.<br /> <br /> Keeping independence as a big faction isn't the same as keeping independence as a small clan or bloodline, and there is no private matters when you're a public figure. They are positioning themselves in the very focus of attention they always avoided, for no gain from their perspective. Their style of political play works better parasitizing another structure instead of making their own private matters into the public matters of their cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T09:47:49-08:00","id":1470447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470358#post1470358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hecata members should really just join the Camarilla or the Sabbat. No (good) reason to stand apart anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joining the Sabbat is just nonsensical, who would want to become a suicidal crazed beast, especially considering the good spot the Hecata are in now. They don't join the Camarilla because they can't until 2028, and don't have a whole lot to gain from it. <br /> <br /> By remaining neutral, the Hecata, to quote CotBG p.145 &quot;...places them in prime position to act as mediators, advisors, and killers, all impartial to the conflicts around them, of course...&quot;. This way, they provide a number of services, financial or necromantical, to Anarchs and Camarilla alike. <br /> <br /> The Hecata are probably one of the most united clans at the moment, even if a lot of bad blood remains, and this gives them a lot of strength to remain as their own minor sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T12:08:17-08:00","id":1470459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul#post1470352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question for more experienced Vampire players.<br /> How do You see Hecata and Sabbat path ? Similarities? <br /> Aren't they not so different? Or I don't see something obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer the question rather than tangents. They're very simular. Effectively paths in v5 are treated as psuado clan so they're effectively very very simular. On a practical level this doesn't really much impact since all Sabbat interactions are intrinsically hyper hostile in v5 and since the Sabbat have been aggressively dumbed down this further limits scope.<br /> The only exceptions is some of the harbingers probably maintain backdoor links with path members and Death and soul might deliberately hunt heceta vampires to accrue Occult lore, like how they might deliberately hunt tremere or lasombra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T13:47:53-08:00","id":1470467,"title":"","content":"If we're talking about the V5 Path of Death and Soul, it's a lot more warlike, focused on killing efficiently and ultimately irreversibly.That's a bit like what Harbingers do, which probably isn't a coincidence. Hecata have more narrowly defined means (a lot of necromancy), but more open ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T22:39:24-08:00","id":1470503,"title":"","content":"Just thinking about it economically. If you have Auspex, Fortitude and necromancy (I won't humour Oblivion, I just won't) you are more valuable in a city where nobody else has those disciplines, and you are going to get more out of other kindred if their specialities aren't Auspex, Fortitude and Necromancy. Unless the Hecata starts recruiting Toreador, Brujah, Nosferatu, Assamites, Tremere, weird bloodlines etc to the point of looking half like the Camarilla, it really isn't in their best interest to form Hecata cities, unless we're talking small 100,000 people cities. <br /> <br /> Before V5, Joining the Camarilla IS the Neutral option, because they're everywhere and everyone worth mentioning. In V5 everyone's IQ and EQ got smashed by a spade and the Rebelion is doing better than The Empire. But before that it'd be less Jyhady to Join what literally everyone else was doing rather than make your own sect with blackjack and hookers (who are your immediate relatives, but Giovanni don't mind). In a post V5 Catastrophe, there still isn't really much good reason to stay apart from everyone else (The Promise of 1520something is fucking stupid and most Giovanni currently active weren't even a twinkling in their grand uncle's eye, it's like sticking to the Magna Carta or Jim Crow long after people have realized some of the ideas aren't so fucking great for modern society) <br /> <br /> Also the Sabbat got destroyed and the Anarchs for whatever fucking reason doesn't seem to have paths anymore so I guess the Hecata can't be on paths because paths are EVIL and only DA SABBAT use em. So, by reading the room, I'd say Hecata got to stick with humanity, even if paths are one of the strongest reasons why they may choose to remain seperate from the Cam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T12:08:50-08:00","id":1470544,"title":"","content":"Is there a precedent for all Hecata cities? Even Florence, presented as a Hecata ruled city, has at least Toreador and Lasombra in a marginalised Camarilla. Furthermore, its Giovanni (and Nagaraja), Samedi and Lamia respectively have Dominate, Obfuscate and Potence; Hecata potentially have 4-6 disciplines, even without simply learning them out of clan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T14:48:38-08:00","id":1470555,"title":"","content":"I'll answer the questions in an objective and simple fashion. I'll also focus on how the two are presented in V5, only pulling from earlier editions to show inspiration for how they are in V5.<br /> <br /> The <b>Hecata</b> are actual my favorite clan. Objectively they are Cappadocians reborn, mixed with the culture and practices of the other necromantic bloodlines. I like how Oblivion is, but hate that Obtenebration was lumped in. Regardless, fun clan/sect/cult.<br /> <br /> <b>The Path of Death and The Soul</b> is <i>interesting</i> to put it simply. In V5 terms, a Path is an alternative form of morality which allows a vampire to exist without the <i><b>burden</b></i> of human ideas. V5 presents them in a similar format as clans to make it easier for Storytellers to create terrifying NPCs. Whereas the Hecata study death in general, The Path of Death studies <b>violent</b> death. Overall, they're bland murder-hobo NPCs with very little RAW nuance.<br /> <br /> If you're noticing a similarity, that's actually for good reason. In earlier editions, the Path of Death and The Soul was originally developed from the Cappadocian morality system known as the <b>Road of Bones</b>. Those who followed the Road were often Cappadocian scholars of death, who studied the very concept of death and what happened after. As time moved on Roads were slowly phased out as the Camarilla encouraged the practice of Humanity alone. Oddly enough, V5 Humanity is very similar to how Roads use to be practiced and developed.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, who formed around the same time as the Camarilla, continued to practice the Roads, but also hypocritically altered them to be even more inhuman as to further separate vampires from humanity. From a meta perspective, we can see Paths become progressively more and more violent as the Editions went on after 2E.<br /> <br /> <b><i>So to put it simply, they're similar because the Hecata's predecessors were the original inventors of the Path before the Sabbat twisted it to fit their own agenda.</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T04:05:27-08:00","id":1470606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470358#post1470358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hecata members should really just join the Camarilla or the Sabbat. No (good) reason to stand apart anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Due to the Promise of 1528, they are not allowed to interfere with the Camarilla in their owed cities, s the Camarillia is not allowed t take away the independence of the Giovanni. They may call themself Hecata now but they and the Cam are still bound by the Promise.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T04:11:02-08:00","id":1470608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470606#post1470606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Due to the Promise of 1528, they are not allowed to interfere with the Camarilla in their owed cities, s the Camarillia is not allowed t take away the independence of the Giovanni. They may call themself Hecata now but they and the Cam are still bound by the Promise.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of laws that nobody follows because there isn't a good reason to. This is one of them. Actually this law is baffling and silly and... really something that should've just been forgotten about (or retconned out of existence.)<br /> <br /> Also this only bounds the Giovanni and not the other Capadocians, their descendents, or the Nagaraja that aren't at all related, who presumably all hid within the other sects. The Giovanni remnants conspiring with the rest of the Hecata is in direct violation of the treaty...<br /> <br /> Yeah the more I think about it the more I'm amazed at how fucking stupid it all is. I feel it oozes smugness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-16-2021, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T04:18:32-08:00","id":1470609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470606#post1470606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to the Promise of 1528, they are not allowed to interfere with the Camarilla in their owed cities, s the Camarillia is not allowed t take away the independence of the Giovanni. They may call themself Hecata now but they and the Cam are still bound by the Promise.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is debatable because we don't know if there is any binding magic to the pact, so it would pretty much depend on their legal vision and disposition to aggrieve a weakened Camarilla. And for me, the very notion of declaring a city a Hecata domain is doing so, so they're either not actually doing nothing with their new sect-like status, or already breaking the Promise anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, it is not just a change of name. The Giovanni may be bound by the Promise, but the other members of the Hecata definitely aren't and can do whatever they want about it, it would be ridiculous to think that the new alliance forces them all to follow on the pacts that the Giovanni made. Their leader, by the way, isn't a Giovanni, the Capuchin may be a lot of people, but all suspects without exception are old Cappadocians, unbound by the Promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:50:36-08:00","id":1470623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470609#post1470609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is debatable because we don't know if there is any binding magic to the pact, so it would pretty much depend on their legal vision and disposition to aggrieve a weakened Camarilla. And for me, the very notion of declaring a city a Hecata domain is doing so, so they're either not actually doing nothing with their new sect-like status, or already breaking the Promise anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, it is not just a change of name. The Giovanni may be bound by the Promise, but the other members of the Hecata definitely aren't and can do whatever they want about it, it would be ridiculous to think that the new alliance forces them all to follow on the pacts that the Giovanni made. Their leader, by the way, isn't a Giovanni, the Capuchin may be a lot of people, but all suspects without exception are old Cappadocians, unbound by the Promise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking a parallel from IR, the Hecata would probably be considered a &quot;successor State&quot; of the Giovanni Clan: from the outside, the rise of the Cult of the Capuchine would just be seen as a coup. If the Capuchin dooesn't denounce the Promise, the new Hecata would just inherit the treaty... And it would of course be very unwise of him to denounce a non aggression pack three years before its expiry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T07:31:04-08:00","id":1470626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470623#post1470623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking a parallel from IR, the Hecata would probably be considered a &quot;successor State&quot; of the Giovanni Clan: from the outside, the rise of the Cult of the Capuchine would just be seen as a coup. If the Capuchin dooesn't denounce the Promise, the new Hecata would just inherit the treaty... And it would of course be very unwise of him to denounce a non aggression pack three years before its expiry.</div> </div> </div> </div>If their goal is just to be independent, sure.<br /> <br /> But if their goal is to set aside the way Augustus was doing things and eye for their future, them approaching the weakened Camarilla to offer help while it isn't in a position to demand much is better than keep the pact in place just to be attacked after it expires and the Cam had time to strength itself.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that while the Hecata <b>can</b> strengthen itself to take the brunt, it is just unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Again, the simple question is: given their goals and proclivities, why does the Hecata wants to be Independent? Why go through all the trouble? I see a lot for them to gain from gong Cam, or even Anarch now. Nothing to lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T11:33:56-08:00","id":1470648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470428#post1470428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The risk is surely of running into the Kyasid problem, &quot;<i>I just sit there and read for the next 300 years</i>&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I always fund this amusing and frankly very stupid &quot;problem&quot;<br /> To sit and read (or study) for the next 300 years, you need a well equiped library; tomes, grimoires, scrolls, tablets, and so on, not to mention the artifacts (or members of different species) to study<br /> And gathering those takes time, actually very long time! Buy it, steal it, bargain for it, in my humble oppinion, your avarage Kiasyd is more like a Lara Croft or Indiana Jones like &quot;adventurer&quot;, treasure hunter, like Becket, always on the filed, searching documents and facts, no matter what is the Kiasyd's field of interest, humanity, cainite lore, arcane, nodist lore, Lillith, Lupin (or Garou), ghost and underword (some of us remeber they used to have necromancy...) or the Abyss, his fae roots, there are TONS of opportunity to NOT to just read for the next 300 years... every Kiasyd (even the bar mixer subtype intrduced in V20; dont forget they need... materials to experient after all, that eastern european '89 midget sumo wrestler's blood is hard to get!) main focus is gathering Knowledge thus logically could and should always be on the field, around dig sites, ruins, and so on. Most of the Mytherceria's powers not really works in your lbirary, sitting, the basic ones, like fodlerol require... well.. someone who talks to you to detect the lie, detecting fae magic, the knowledge stelaing powers, even the riddle phantastiq (I'm a sadist GM and always require my Kiasyd player actually KNOW the answer to his own riddle, research the subject and so on...) are designed to be used on others, on the field so to speak (some of the older ones, like Earth Swords are even very combat oriented )it<br /> So a young Kiasyd, but even an ancillae are an ideal if not the best party member on par with a Nosferatu when it comes to curiosity or usefulness! It not only willing to gather that obscure knowladge he wants and have a deeply rooted need ,dare I say, to satisfy his thirst for knowledge, but even manipulate his coterie/pack to help him, or offer favors for his help, be a social butterfly even in an elysium, or raid a Tremere Library with a Sabbat war party, visit Courts as an Independent, just to name a few<br /> Actually, when it comes to the Kiasyd, in my humble oppinion the LAST thing they do is the sitting around for decades reading. Elders, maybe... but thats true for every elder? A young Kiasyd or even aan older one? Have a tons of work to fill his library and maybe after that will have time to sit and read...<br /> But this is only my two cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 12-16-2021, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T17:10:57-08:00","id":1470671,"title":"","content":"So when the Promise ends, what do people think the Hecata will do? Will the Hecata choose to join either the Camarilla or the Anarchs or will they officially set themselves up as a full rival sect to the other two? There really aren't any major groups in either the Camarilla or the Anarchs who particularly detest the Giovanni/Hecata (not like the Assamites and the Followers of Set anyway), so if the Hecata offered to join the Camarilla or the Anarchs, I think they'd probably be welcomed and might even get some very good terms considering the amount of resources (money, revenants, lore, etc) they could bring with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T19:40:18-08:00","id":1470684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470671#post1470671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when the Promise ends, what do people think the Hecata will do? Will the Hecata choose to join either the Camarilla or the Anarchs or will they officially set themselves up as a full rival sect to the other two? There really aren't any major groups in either the Camarilla or the Anarchs who particularly detest the Giovanni/Hecata (not like the Assamites and the Followers of Set anyway), so if the Hecata offered to join the Camarilla or the Anarchs, I think they'd probably be welcomed and might even get some very good terms considering the amount of resources (money, revenants, lore, etc) they could bring with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rival sect. My headcannon is that's what they'll do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T02:22:37-08:00","id":1470698,"title":"","content":"I don't think they'd join the carmarilla is circling the drain in V5 and relentlessly inept. I suspect they're just going to wait and see how events pan out, then again the writings all over the place so they're most likely just going to do something the writters consider dramatic such as resume either of the previous 'plans'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-17-2021, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T09:14:23-08:00","id":1470786,"title":"","content":"There's no sect in V5 that can guarantee security for the rest of the century. Hecata note they're uniquely not at war with any clan or sect and they mean to keep it that way. If they join one, they'll be targeted by the other two. They're not going to take over the world as an independent faction, but they aren't trying to, they want to survive long enough to watch it die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T14:10:20-08:00","id":1470805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470555#post1470555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll answer the questions in an objective and simple fashion. I'll also focus on how the two are presented in V5, only pulling from earlier editions to show inspiration for how they are in V5.<br /> <br /> The <b>Hecata</b> are actual my favorite clan. Objectively they are Cappadocians reborn, mixed with the culture and practices of the other necromantic bloodlines. I like how Oblivion is, but hate that Obtenebration was lumped in. Regardless, fun clan/sect/cult.<br /> <br /> <b>The Path of Death and The Soul</b> is <i>interesting</i> to put it simply. In V5 terms, a Path is an alternative form of morality which allows a vampire to exist without the <i><b>burden</b></i> of human ideas. V5 presents them in a similar format as clans to make it easier for Storytellers to create terrifying NPCs. Whereas the Hecata study death in general, The Path of Death studies <b>violent</b> death. Overall, they're bland murder-hobo NPCs with very little RAW nuance.<br /> <br /> If you're noticing a similarity, that's actually for good reason. In earlier editions, the Path of Death and The Soul was originally developed from the Cappadocian morality system known as the <b>Road of Bones</b>. Those who followed the Road were often Cappadocian scholars of death, who studied the very concept of death and what happened after. As time moved on Roads were slowly phased out as the Camarilla encouraged the practice of Humanity alone. Oddly enough, V5 Humanity is very similar to how Roads use to be practiced and developed.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, who formed around the same time as the Camarilla, continued to practice the Roads, but also hypocritically altered them to be even more inhuman as to further separate vampires from humanity. From a meta perspective, we can see Paths become progressively more and more violent as the Editions went on after 2E.<br /> <br /> <b><i>So to put it simply, they're similar because the Hecata's predecessors were the original inventors of the Path before the Sabbat twisted it to fit their own agenda.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might be the first thing about V5 I've ever heard that has made me genuinely angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T00:41:13-08:00","id":1470827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470805#post1470805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this might be the first thing about V5 I've ever heard that has made me genuinely angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not following you; Explain why this makes you angry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T09:31:18-08:00","id":1470861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470827#post1470827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not following you; Explain why this makes you angry?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be a bit more specific, I'm referring to the fact that the &quot;Path of Death&quot; was converted into an obsession with fighting, not with *death*. Not to say that an old-school member of the PoDS wouldn't be a horrifying serial killer, but I imagine a lot of the more gruesome murder-hobo tendencies would fade over time, as randomly performing &quot;experiments&quot; gives way to more specific research. There was so much you could do with it, so many directions to go with it. Now it basically just sounds like someone who obsessively studies weapons and anatomy, and that just hacks of so much good stuff IMO.<br /> <br /> Path of Death of the Soul is one of my favourite Paths, so hearing that they shoved it into a meatgrinder just to churn out an extra helping of slasher-horror that the Sabbat really didn't need grinds my gears a bit. I'd previously heard discussion of the Sabbat being pushed back into the dumb-antagonist-only slot, but this is a more concrete example of them actively wiping out any alternatives. I like the philosophy of the Paths and the Roads, and while there have been plenty of things that I've disagreed with regarding V5, actively trying to destroy the esoteric inhuman philosophies of the Path of Enlightenment is probably the first one that really pisses me off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T04:02:56-08:00","id":1470922,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> Than you'll be happy to know what he said wasn't accurate at all. The Path of Death and the Soul in V5 is, by far, the most esoteric and intelectual Path. They are not concerned with violent death, they are concerned with learning and developing new ways to strike at the Antediluvians, and their pawns. Experiments are likewise still a thing, as followers of the Path develop Blood-borne pathogens, monstrous ghouls, or spectral anchors to harrass their enemies. To quote the Sabbat book:<br /> &quot;The premise of the Path of Death and the Soul is to study, understand, and master death so that destroyed enemies remain dead. As the Sabbat understands it, the hated Antediluvians \u201chave power over life and death\u201d according to the Book of Nod, raising the question of whether or not, should the Sabbat destroy one of the Third Generation, that vampire will stay dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Followers of the Path of Death and the Soul are systematic thinkers, and give great consideration to the outcomes of their plans. They act with calculated precision, leaving as little to chance as possible, from knowing exactly who they\u2019re sending into a conflict to projecting how many Cainites a tiny domain may sustain three decades after claiming it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Originating as students of death \u2013 the ultimate end of all life \u2013 the Path has hence taken on a broader role for the Black Hand as what might be best described as an occult research and development function.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T09:05:01-08:00","id":1470936,"title":"","content":"Would you see one sitting in a terminal care home, quietly scribbling away as people die of natural causes, the &quot;control&quot; group to compare with when they offer to euthanize other patients?<br /> <br /> It sounds like things may be better than I feared, but Path of Death and the Soul was developed from the Cappadocian Road of Bones, and anything that is lopped off and ignored simply for the purpose of focusing on fighting the Antediluvians is something of a corruption. A lot of what I liked about Death and the Soul had to do with the similarity to Metamorphosis: if there is any interest beyond knowledge for its own sake, its in the potential for growth and self-improvement that the knowledge provides. Making the primary focus on &quot;keeping your enemies dead&quot; is a rejection of the more interesting roots of the Path, IMO. And again, I'm not saying those subjects don't fit into the Path, but rather that important elements seem to have been discarded in favour of this focus on killing the enemy. And that makes some sense for the Sabbat as a bunch of fundamentalist crusaders I guess, but it messes with things I liked personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T11:39:46-08:00","id":1470938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470922#post1470922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> Than you'll be happy to know what he said wasn't accurate at all. The Path of Death and the Soul in V5 is, by far, the most esoteric and intelectual Path. They are not concerned with violent death, they are concerned with learning and developing new ways to strike at the Antediluvians, and their pawns. Experiments are likewise still a thing, as followers of the Path develop Blood-borne pathogens, monstrous ghouls, or spectral anchors to harrass their enemies. To quote the Sabbat book:<br /> &quot;The premise of the Path of Death and the Soul is to study, understand, and master death so that destroyed enemies remain dead. As the Sabbat understands it, the hated Antediluvians \u201chave power over life and death\u201d according to the Book of Nod, raising the question of whether or not, should the Sabbat destroy one of the Third Generation, that vampire will stay dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Followers of the Path of Death and the Soul are systematic thinkers, and give great consideration to the outcomes of their plans. They act with calculated precision, leaving as little to chance as possible, from knowing exactly who they\u2019re sending into a conflict to projecting how many Cainites a tiny domain may sustain three decades after claiming it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Originating as students of death \u2013 the ultimate end of all life \u2013 the Path has hence taken on a broader role for the Black Hand as what might be best described as an occult research and development function.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry mate, as much as they can make it <i><b>seem</b></i> scholarly, you also left out the Ethics of those on this path which make them much more violent than their past counterparts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u25a0 Leave no survivors at the conclusion of violent conflict.<br /> \u25a0 Investigate the relics and remains of death \u2013 personal, historical, occult \u2013 in order to discern the details of how the conflict ended and its existential outcomes.<br /> \u25a0 Hasten death\u2019s arrival, from humblest insect to the much-lamented flower of human life. </div> </div> </div>- V5 Sabbat page 25<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Study death in all its permutations.<br /> \u2022 Determine when death occurs; define it.<br /> \u2022 Search for a purpose for death and the life that prefaces it.<br /> \u2022 Quantify the differences of death by various causes.<br /> \u2022 Achieve a comfort with death and unlife \u2014 distinguish between damnation and salvation.<br /> \u2022 Hasten death\u2019s arrival, should it seem to be unnaturally delayed. </div> </div> </div>- V20 Core Rulebook page 319<br /> <br /> If you look at Ethics alone, you'll notice some noticeable changes. <i>&quot;Hasten death\u2019s arrival, should it seem to be unnaturally delayed.&quot;</i> has become &quot;\u200bHasten death\u2019s arrival, from humblest insect to the much-lamented flower of human life.&quot;<br /> <br /> This change alone shows the difference in attitudes V5 Sabbat then previous editions of the sect, outside of 1e. The Sabbat has always been violent and monstrous, but this has been exaugurated in V5. You'll also notice that in V20 specifically ethics all revolve around study of death in general, V5 ethics seem to be more concerned with the aftermath of conflicts and not so much dying in general.<br /> <br /> With all that said, I do have to point out that you are correct in that the Path is still primarily thinkers. Not only that but it appears they're the only path in Sabbat V5 that has a brain. This is ironic considering the Path of Caine, which use to be just as scholarly as the Path of Bones, is also presented in the same book on page 21.<br /> <br /> So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>, to answer your question in the above post: <b><i>Maybe?</i></b> As they're presented in V5, the Path of Death and the Soul is more preoccupied with killing things and figuring out how to keep them dead. Paradoxically however, the Path seems to prefer the theater of conflict, and will avoid it whenever possible. This is odd considering their V5 ethics. They're just as cold and calculating as presented in earlier editions apparently, as presented by the text on page 25. However, their ethics seem to imply a preference into the study of conflict, and the resulting deaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T13:08:46-08:00","id":1470945,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26764_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26764\" data-vbnamecard=\"26764\">Vilenecromancer</a> the question was somewhat rhetorical, and directed more specifically at <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a> since they had been responding to me in particular. But yeah, I agree that what you just described sounds like, at best, a &quot;maybe&quot; for the scenario I provided. That contrast in the Ethics pointed out really hits it: &quot;hasten death when it seems unnaturally delayed&quot; leaves a lot more room for nuance and interpretation than &quot;hasten death, for everything, period.&quot;<br /> <br /> One thing that I was reflecting on before posting initially was the PoDS ethic that, in my opinion, had the most potential to drive excessive bloodshed: &quot;not killing when useful or necessary.&quot; Depending on how you view it, that could arguably be reason to kill literally everything that you come across, as who knows which deaths might reveal new secrets, unusual anatomy in an autopsy, etc. But that's part of where my discussion of &quot;diminishing returns&quot; and such came in above. After killing a bunch of people in horrible ways, getting a handle on anatomy by studying their corpses, the base level of knowledge will have been acquired, and most future killing will be determined by specific values. It leaves room for discretion, whether killing someone today or killing them another day might have the most potential for learning.<br /> <br /> But &quot;hasten death for everyone&quot; is much more indiscriminate, and leaves less room for the kind of consideration described above. Going back to the terminal care home, there's maybe an argument that their death has been &quot;unnaturally delayed.&quot; But if dealing death without qualification is your primary consideration, then you're probably just going to end up with a care home full of corpses after a single night.<br /> <br /> To go back and address the OP very quickly, the difference between the Hecata and the Path of Death is that one is a clan, the other a philosophy. In fact, there are probably members of the Hecata who still follow the Road of Bones or the non-murderhobo version of the Path of Death, because the Cappadocians *invented* it. Maybe the V5 rules don't handle it very well, but there shouldn't be any reason you couldn't make a Hecata member of the Sabbat following their Path of Death, from a lore perspective anyways (ps. especially since, as noted above, many Hecata members view death and necromancy more as tools than subjects of study).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 12-20-2021, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T13:10:39-08:00","id":1470946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470352-hecata-vs-path-of-death-and-soul?p=1470938#post1470938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry mate, as much as they can make it <i><b>seem</b></i> scholarly, you also left out the Ethics of those on this path which make them much more violent than their past counterparts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is scholarly, compared to the rest of the Sabbat anyway. They are more violent because the Sabbat itself is more violent and no longer playing Religious Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - V5 Sabbat page 25<br /> <br /> <br /> - V20 Core Rulebook page 319<br /> <br /> If you look at Ethics alone, you'll notice some noticeable changes. <i>&quot;Hasten death\u2019s arrival, should it seem to be unnaturally delayed.&quot;</i> has become &quot;\u200bHasten death\u2019s arrival, from humblest insect to the much-lamented flower of human life.&quot;<br /> <br /> This change alone shows the difference in attitudes V5 Sabbat then previous editions of the sect, outside of 1e. The Sabbat has always been violent and monstrous, but this has been exaugurated in V5. You'll also notice that in V20 specifically ethics all revolve around study of death in general, V5 ethics seem to be more concerned with the aftermath of conflicts and not so much dying in general. </div> </div> </div>Because they aren't studying death as its own natural thing, if you were going to do that you might as well be a Hecata with Humanity in V5. They study death to use it as a weapon against the Antediluvians, to channel death and decay against them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With all that said, I do have to point out that you are correct in that the Path is still primarily thinkers. Not only that but it appears they're the only path in Sabbat V5 that has a brain. This is ironic considering the Path of Caine, which use to be just as scholarly as the Path of Bones, is also presented in the same book on page 21. </div> </div> </div>Its clear that they wanted each Paths to be very distinct from one another. Hunters, Sadists, Scholars and Conquerors. Hence why the Path of Night was made a variation of the Cathari, and Metamorphosis is likely a variation on Death and the Soul, considering Fleshweld Ghouls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>, to answer your question in the above post: <b><i>Maybe?</i></b> As they're presented in V5, the Path of Death and the Soul is more preoccupied with killing things and figuring out how to keep them dead. Paradoxically however, the Path seems to prefer the theater of conflict, and will avoid it whenever possible. This is odd considering their V5 ethics. They're just as cold and calculating as presented in earlier editions apparently, as presented by the text on page 25. However, their ethics seem to imply a preference into the study of conflict, and the resulting deaths. </div> </div> </div>Its not paradoxical. They avoid conflict because their greatest powers is attacking with Spectres, Diseases, Sorcery and monstrous Ghouls from afar. If they enter the conflict themselves, its because its absolutely necessary to their plans, and that means none of their enemies will walk out alive. They study the afterward of their plans in conflict, see how their diseases affected the enemy, how long their ghouls endured and whether the spectres served well.<br /> <br /> &quot;Once the Blood starts to flow, the Reapers are content to observe, allowing their plans to play out while collating learnings from the results. They are not so detached as to avoid first-hand observations, however, but make sure to do so as a pack, or otherwise surround themselves with loyal security.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}